Third-party components under other licences
-------------------------------------------

The deploy kit (kit/) contains no third-party code. It references stock images
that its users pull from their publishers under their own licences (Authelia
and Caddy: Apache-2.0; PostgreSQL with pgvector: PostgreSQL Licence; Valkey:
BSD-3-Clause; MongoDB 4.4: SSPL-1.0, run as Cerea's internal database and not
offered as a service); kit/README.md lists them, with the tools its optional
backup sidecar installs.

libvips, as the prebuilt @img/sharp-libvips-* binaries (and the libvips inside
@img/sharp-win32-* and @img/sharp-wasm32) installed as optional dependencies
of sharp: LGPL-3.0-or-later. They are loaded dynamically by sharp at runtime
and are not modified.
  libvips source: https://github.com/libvips/libvips
  binary packaging: https://github.com/lovell/sharp-libvips

The galopin agent binaries (agent/) include the Go standard library
(BSD-3-Clause), github.com/coder/websocket (ISC) and github.com/creack/pty
(MIT); the licence texts are in agent/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES and travel with
every binary (`galopin licenses` prints them).

